# SPECTRA - .gitignore
#
# Status: session one. This file is the thing being delivered; everything it
# names is "not started".
#
# Two standing rules from the specification govern this file:
#
#   1. Part II section 73.11: a source path that fails the load-bearing audit
#      (ORPHAN_SOURCE) is NEVER silenced by adding it here. Adding a language
#      directory to this file to dodge `make polyglot-audit` is a defect.
#   2. Part I section 32.9: nothing under data/generated/, data/runs/ or
#      bench/results/ is ever committed.
#
# Anything committed must be reproducible offline from a clean clone. If a path
# is ignored here, no gate may depend on its presence.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Spec-mandated generated data paths (Part I section 32.2, section 32.9)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/ is ignored wholesale EXCEPT the two committed subtrees:
#   data/fixtures/  small, byte-stable bundles for unit tests  (TRACKED)
#   data/golden/    certificates + expected checker output     (TRACKED)
data/*
!data/fixtures/
!data/golden/

# Belt and braces: named explicitly so a future `!data/**` never resurrects them.
data/generated/
data/runs/

# Benchmark results are regenerated by `make benchmark` / `make bench-degrade`.
bench/results/

# Scratch output roots used by the determinism repro targets (Part II section 58).
out/
bin/

# Toolchain OCI tarball blobs. Part II section 74.9 table: "committed by hash
# reference; blobs mirrored out-of-band". images.lock IS committed; the tars are not.
cas/oci/*.tar
cas/oci/*.tar.zst
cas/tmp/

# TODO(decision): artifacts/ is NOT ignored. `artifacts/polyglot/audit.json` is
# the only admissible source of the polyglot counts quoted in README and docs
# (Part II section 73.11), so it must be readable from a clean clone with the
# network off. If a future session decides those counts should be regenerated
# rather than read, ignore `artifacts/` here and make the README block a build
# step instead.

