# uv.lock IS committed (Part I section 33.4). Do not add it here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rust
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
.cargo/registry/
.cargo/git/

# Cargo.lock IS committed (workspace with binaries). Do not add it here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Go
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
go.work.sum.tmp

# NOTE: repo-root vendor/ is deliberately NOT ignored. Part II section 73.8
# marks vendor/** linguist-vendored, and polyglot.toml declares offline_source
# paths under vendor/, which only works if the tree is tracked. Part I section
# 32.9 ("do not vendor third-party source") is narrowed by Part II section 74:
# offline bundles are real. Per-ecosystem vendor dirs that ARE build output
# must be ignored by name, not by a blanket vendor/ rule.

# go.work and go.work.sum ARE committed (Part I section 32.2). Do not add them here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node / TypeScript
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.npm/
.yarn/
*.tsbuildinfo
.next/
.nuxt/
.vite/
.turbo/
web/**/dist/
web/**/build/
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/
.playwright/

# pnpm-lock.yaml IS committed. Do not add it here.

